    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d351">

                <pb facs="0476" n="402" sameAs="frus:frus1866p1/pg402"/>

                <head>Mr. Clay to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 102.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">St. Petersburg, Russia,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-02-22"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 22, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I take the liberty of sending you a report
                    of the anniversary dinner (18th of February instant, translated from the French
                    of the St. Petersburg Journal, the official paper of to-day) of the Marine
                    Assembly. Mr. J. Curtin and myself were informally invited, but the whole
                    proceeding, I understand, was approved by his imperial Majesty the Grand Duke
                    Constantine.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>C. M. CLAY.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William h. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
                <postscript>
                    <p>P. S.—This society is a regulation assembly of the whole marine.</p>
                    <p rendition="#right">CLAY.</p>
                </postscript>



                <xi:include href="d351-a1.xml" xpointer="d351-a1"/>
            </div>
